The package's `BENCH_ORDER.md` is source advisory only. It does not supersede the hash-bound native experiment-readiness queue at `data/governance/inventory_v5_experiment_readiness_closure_queue_20260812.json` (24,578 bytes / `ff228b72a155e14902416b1de8d92e75f7302123c80f292abfc85adbd997ee2a`). That queue keeps CLR-001 2-Acetyl Pyrazine and CLR-002 Lemonile as the first direct experiment gates; Helional and Heliotropal remain non-direct, execution-unauthorized closure actions. The native next hypothesis remains `H_BIN_MIXTURE_BASELINE_AFTER_IDENTITY_CLOSURE`, prospective only and physical-execution unauthorized.

